// expect-error: NITPICK-MACRO-003
//
// EXPANSION HAS TWO BOUNDS AND THIS IS THE OTHER ONE (D-057). The iteration bound
// stops a macro that expands into itself for ever; this stops a SINGLE expansion
// whose body nests deeper than the clone will follow. They are different mistakes
// — one program does not terminate, the other is too complicated — and reporting
// both as one budget would make the second look like the first.
//
// NESTED OPERATORS, NOT NESTED PARENTHESES. The first version of this file used
// 600 parentheses and expanded cleanly: parentheses GROUP, and grouping builds no
// node, so the clone followed a body one level deep. The bound counts nodes, so
// the test has to build them.
//
// GENERATED RATHER THAN WRITTEN, because the bound is 512 and a person does not
// nest six hundred additions by hand. That is the point: the bound sits far above
// anything anybody means, so reaching it says the program is not one.
mod:too_deep;

